@startuml state_event_replay_cursors
!include ../../../design/theme.iuml

title Event Replay, Cursor, and Gap States

[*] --> NoSubscriber

NoSubscriber --> LiveSubscriber : subscribe(live-only)
NoSubscriber --> ReplaySubscriber : subscribe(replayable class)
NoSubscriber --> CursorSubscriber : subscribe(cursor runtime class)

ReplaySubscriber --> ReplayingHistory : snapshot bounded ring
ReplayingHistory --> LiveSubscriber : replay complete
ReplayingHistory --> GapReported : ring overflow detected
GapReported --> LiveSubscriber : deliver gap marker + continue live

CursorSubscriber --> CursorActive : assign cursor/sequence
CursorActive --> CursorLagging : consumer falls behind
CursorLagging --> GapReported : queue/ring overflow or skipped range
CursorLagging --> CursorActive : catches up

LiveSubscriber --> DroppingEvents : best-effort queue full
DroppingEvents --> LiveSubscriber : increment drop counter / coalesce gap

LiveSubscriber --> [*] : unsubscribe/disconnect
CursorActive --> [*] : unsubscribe/disconnect
ReplaySubscriber --> [*] : unsubscribe/disconnect

note right of ReplaySubscriber
Lifecycle/control events are candidates
for eager bounded replay.
end note

note right of CursorSubscriber
High-rate runtime telemetry uses
cursors/gaps, not guaranteed full replay.
end note

@enduml
